  "body": "#870: a Makera Z1 user cut air on their first program because they hadn't understood where the origin was. Then it \"took a while to find out how to actually save the setting, as the 'set origin' button is crammed next to a lot of other options\".\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0, PROCESS_VERSION 29; merged with upstream main at 62a2c93a.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Set origin in the footer.** The WCS page's apply button leaves the page body (where it shared a row with *Level*, among the quarter turns) and moves into the property pane's fixed footer, beside *Close* (`egui_app::wcs_footer`). Every other page keeps its plain *Close*.\n- **Pending edits are flagged.** While the typed X/Y/Z or angles differ from the placed WCS, the footer shows **Origin not applied** in the warning ink.\n  - The position is compared to 1e-9 mm. The angles are compared as rotations, so yaw 360 is not an edit. A non-finite field reads as pending.\n  - The drafts survive a close and reopen, so closing loses nothing silently. Closing does not apply them either.\n- **The origin in words.** A new pure module, `app::setup_origin`, places the origin against the box the page anchors on (the stock box, else the model's bounds).\n  - A point on one of the 27 anchor points is named, e.g. `top of stock, front-left corner`, `top of stock, centre` or `mid-height of stock, front edge, centred`.\n  - Any other point is given as signed distances from the box's left side, front and top, so it never claims a corner it is not on.\n  - The WCS page states it under its heading: `G54 origin: top of stock, front-left corner (X0 Y0 Z0)`. The setup sheet gains an `origin:` line under the WCS numbers.\n- **Viewport marker:** the WCS axis triad already marks the origin; nothing was added.\n- **Docs:** `docs/user-guide/work-origin.md`, a short page on where the origin is shown and how to change it.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/870-wcs-set-origin-footer.md`.\n\n**Overlap with #759** (@mkinney, open draft, `conflicts`): it splits the WCS page body out of `pages.rs` into `wcs_page.rs` and keeps its own *Set Origin* in the quarter-turn rows. This PR touches the page body in one place only, removing that button. The new code lives in its own files (`wcs_footer.rs`, `setup_origin.rs`). Whichever lands second drops the body button and calls `wcs_footer::origin_line` from the page.\n\n## How it was tested\n\nNew pinning tests:\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/wcs_footer.rs` (structural: painted text, AccessKit labels, coarse placement):\n  - `the_page_says_where_the_origin_is_in_words`\n  - `set_origin_sits_in_the_footer_beside_close_and_nowhere_else`: one row, Set origin before Close, below the page body, exactly one apply button, no flag on a fresh page.\n  - `a_typed_origin_is_flagged_until_set_origin_applies_it`: the flag appears, a click on Set origin places the typed X and clears it, and yaw 360 does not raise it.\n- `app::setup_origin` unit tests: `every_anchor_point_is_named`, `a_point_off_the_anchors_is_given_as_distances_never_as_a_corner`, `a_non_finite_origin_or_box_says_so`.\n- `crates/app/tests/setup_wcs.rs`: `the_setup_sheet_says_where_the_origin_is_in_words` (corner, centre, off-anchor).\n\nTwo existing ui tests got a taller window, 1280 x 900 instead of 720. The new origin line makes the WCS page one to two rows taller, and at 720 px the bottom of the page scrolls under the footer. The page scrolls; nothing is lost.\n- `one_wcs::the_wcs_page_shows_the_work_offset_dropdown_and_no_setups_page_pointer`: its bottom note was out of view.\n- `origin_page_shows_the_anchor_grid_and_arms_pick_mode`: its SE cell click missed.\n\nGates on 8b850a18:\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui` (CWD `crates/ui`): all green. The lib has 596 passed and 5 ignored; every integration binary passes.\n- App suites that read the setup sheet or the WCS: `setup_wcs`, `setup_sheet`, `rotated_wcs`, `setup_align`, `program_entry`, `inverted_axis_display`, `setup_stock_source`: all pass. `cargo test -p camcraft-app --lib setup_origin`: 3 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- No snapshot PNG touched.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Not looked at in the running app. The layout is pinned structurally only.\n- On a rotated or aligned setup (#326), \"left\" and \"front\" are the world box's, as the anchor grid's compass names already are.\n- The release-lane pixel snapshots were not run. If one frames the WCS page, it moves at the cut's regeneration.\n\nChangelog: WCS page: Set origin sits in the footer beside Close, unapplied edits are flagged, and the page and setup sheet say where the origin is in words (\"top of stock, front-left corner\") (#870)\n\nEffort: medium (the issue's label). Not escalated.\n\nFixes #870\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
